    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. Build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an `initials` field to the owner GET response, computed as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (`\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`).\n\nI followed the existing `displayName` idiom exactly, which keeps structural impact minimal \u2014 two edits, no new methods, no growth of any class:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field), directly mirroring `displayName`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = ...)` line to `toOwnerDto`. The method's cyclomatic complexity stays 1, and only one line changed.\n\nNo behaviour was added to any existing method body and no class grew, so the `WMC_other * CC * changed_lines` cost stays low (one 1-line annotation on a CC-1 method, across two files).",
